# The circuit compiler's messages, as clang words them (file:line:col), on broken netlists (Inputs/broken-*.cir):
# fminus prints them and exits 1 without generating anything.
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-parse.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PARSE --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-plan.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAN --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-feedback.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FEEDBACK
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-ports.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PORTS --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-cycle.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CYCLE --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-singular.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SINGULAR --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-nooutput.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOOUTPUT --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-negative.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NEGATIVE --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/play-broken.fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAY --implicit-check-not=error: --implicit-check-not="not found"

# PARSE:      {{.*}}broken-parse.cir:7:19: error: 'AC 1': a V source is DC: the signal is .input's
# PARSE-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-parse.cir:8:19: error: unknown pot 'tonee' (the pots: tone)
# PARSE-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-parse.cir:9:20: error: the exponent of '^' is an integer from 0 to 8
# PARSE-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-parse.cir:10:22: error: 'RS=-10': RS is 0 or a resistance from 1e-30 to 1e30 ohms
# PARSE-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-parse.cir:11:9: error: '.method bdf2' is not supported yet (Phase 1)
# PARSE-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-parse.cir:12:1: error: '.subckt' is not supported yet
# PARSE-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-parse.cir:13:1: error: unknown directive '.foo'

# PLAN:      {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:6:1: error: node 'f1' has one connection (R6); a node needs two
# PLAN-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:7:1: error: node 'z2' reaches ground only through capacitors (C3, C9): its DC voltage is undefined (add 10meg to ground)
# PLAN-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:9:16: error: unknown model '1N4148X' (the models: 1N914; built in: 1N914, 1N4148)
# PLAN-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:10:16: error: unknown model '1N4148X' (the models: 1N914; built in: 1N914, 1N4148)
# PLAN-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:12:1: error: diodes D3 and D4 in series through node 'k' have different models (1N914, 1N4148): a series string is of one model

# FEEDBACK: {{.*}}broken-feedback.cir:7:1: error: op amp XU1 has no negative feedback: an ideal op amp needs one

# PORTS: {{.*}}broken-ports.cir:5:1: error: block 1 has 2 nonlinear ports (D1|D2, D3|D4): multi-port Newton is Phase 2

# CYCLE: {{.*}}broken-cycle.cir:7:1: error: a feedback loop around XU1 crosses blocks: not supported yet (Phase 2)

# SINGULAR: {{.*}}broken-singular.cir:5:1: error: block 1 (XU1, XU2, R1, R2, ...): its equations are singular (nothing determines V(o2)): an op amp without negative feedback, or a node cut off from the rest

# NOOUTPUT: {{.*}}broken-nooutput.cir: error: the netlist has no .output

# NEGATIVE: {{.*}}broken-negative.cir:7:1: error: port D1|D2 sees a negative resistance (K = -123.2 ohm at 22.05 kHz): positive feedback around XU1 is not supported yet

# The synth path's refusals (an OTA, G<name> n+ n- OTA nc+ nc- gain, and law inputs, .input NAME - kind=cv|current):
# a current input without its range and a law input outside an OTA's gain (the parser's), two OTAs in one block, an
# open-loop OTA, diode and OTA ports in one region, and omega3 asked of an OTA (the plan's).
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-laws.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LAWS --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-otas.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OTAS --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-openloop.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OPEN --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-mixed.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MIXED --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-omega.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OMEGA --match-full-lines

# LAWS:      {{.*}}broken-laws.cir:3:19: error: law input 'iabc' is a current: it needs its range in amps, range=lo:hi (as range=10u:2m)
# LAWS-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-laws.cir:6:27: error: law input 'cv' in R1's value: a law input enters an OTA's gain only (pot-as-port is Phase 2)

# OTAS: {{.*}}broken-otas.cir:6:1: error: block 1 has 2 nonlinear ports (G1, G2): multi-port Newton is Phase 2

# OPEN: {{.*}}broken-openloop.cir:8:1: error: OTA G1 has no feedback around it (an open-loop OTA, a VCA): Phase 2

# MIXED: {{.*}}broken-mixed.cir:15:1: error: the oversampled region mixes diode ports (D1|D2) and OTA ports (G1): one solver serves a region (per-family solvers are Phase 2)

# OMEGA: {{.*}}broken-omega.cir:6:1: error: '.solver omega(1)': an OTA's port is solved from the previous step's v: .solver newton(K)

# Phase 1's elements and DC operating point: a loop of a V source and an inductor, and a node only a current source
# and a capacitor reach (the topology's checks); a pair with unequal RS, and a series string of two models (the diode
# forms'); an E whose controls are in two blocks (the partition's); a diode a supply biases (the DC point's: the
# offset formulation is Phase 2's). broken-parse.cir has an AC spec on a V source.
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-dc.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TOPOLOGY --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-diodes.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DIODES --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-controls.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CONTROLS --match-full-lines
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/broken-biased.cir --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BIASED --match-full-lines

# TOPOLOGY:      {{.*}}broken-dc.cir:9:1: error: a loop of voltage sources, E outputs and inductors (V1, L1): its DC current is undefined
# TOPOLOGY-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-dc.cir:11:1: error: node 'x' reaches ground only through capacitors and current sources (I1, C1): its DC voltage is undefined (add 10meg to ground)

# DIODES:      {{.*}}broken-diodes.cir:8:1: error: antiparallel D1|D2 have unequal RS (10 and 5 ohm): a pair shares one series resistor
# DIODES-NEXT: {{.*}}broken-diodes.cir:11:1: error: diodes D3 and D4 in series through node 'm' have different models (1N914, 1N4148): a series string is of one model

# CONTROLS: {{.*}}broken-controls.cir:12:1: error: E1's controls, 'a' and 'b', are in two blocks: an E reads one block's nodes (or its input)

# BIASED: {{.*}}broken-biased.cir:8:1: error: port D1 is biased at DC (0.573 V): biased ports need the offset formulation (Phase 2)

# --emit fm is a netlist's: on an FMinus source it is an error.
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/play.fm --emit fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOTCIR --match-full-lines
# NOTCIR: fminus: --emit fm: {{.*}}play.fm is not a circuit netlist (.cir)

# A warning is not an error: 1M is a milliohm in SPICE, and the netlist still generates.
# RUN: fminus %S/Inputs/milliohm.cir --emit fm -o %t.fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MILLI --match-full-lines
# MILLI: {{.*}}milliohm.cir:5:16: warning: '1M' is 1 milliohm in SPICE; write 1meg for a megohm

# A netlist included twice is generated once: its warning shows once.
# RUN: fminus %S/Inputs/play-twice.fm -o %t.ll 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TWICE --implicit-check-not=warning:
# TWICE: {{.*}}milliohm.cir:5:16: warning: '1M' is 1 milliohm in SPICE; write 1meg for a megohm

# Through #include: the circuit's errors, and no FMinus error after them.
# PLAY: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:6:1: error: node 'f1' has one connection (R6); a node needs two
# PLAY: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:7:1: error: node 'z2' reaches ground only through capacitors (C3, C9): its DC voltage is undefined (add 10meg to ground)
# PLAY: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:9:16: error: unknown model '1N4148X' (the models: 1N914; built in: 1N914, 1N4148)
# PLAY: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:10:16: error: unknown model '1N4148X' (the models: 1N914; built in: 1N914, 1N4148)
# PLAY: {{.*}}broken-plan.cir:12:1: error: diodes D3 and D4 in series through node 'k' have different models (1N914, 1N4148): a series string is of one model

# FMinus's messages on a generated module are re-cited at the netlist's line the generated line comes from
# (Result::lines): play-redefine.fm declares its own module PotClipper before #include "clipper-pot.cir", and the
# module generated from clipper-pot.cir redefines it at the netlist's .title line.
# RUN: not fminus %S/Inputs/play-redefine.fm 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RECITED --match-full-lines
# RECITED:      In file included from {{.*}}play-redefine.fm:7:
# RECITED-NEXT: {{.*}}clipper-pot.cir:3:1: error: redefinition of 'PotClipper' (in the module generated from clipper-pot.cir, line 8)
